.TH DAGonFS 1 "15 November 2026" "DAGonFS" "DAGonFS"
.SH NAME
DAGonFS \- MPI-distributed in-memory filesystem using FUSE3
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mpirun \-np
.I P
.B dagonfs
[\fB\-\-model\fR \fIclient-server\fR|\fIpeer-to-peer\fR]
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-\-log\fR]
.I root
.br
.B DAGonFS_Launcher
[\fIDAGonFS.ini\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR \fIM\fR] [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B DAGonFS
is an in-memory FUSE3 filesystem for temporary workflow data. It coordinates file
data between MPI processes using either a client-server or peer-to-peer model.
It is not durable storage: unmounting or stopping the service discards its contents.
.PP
.B dagonfs
runs on every rank of an MPI job. The deployment model is chosen per volume:
.B client-server
(the default) mounts
.I root
on rank 0;
.B peer-to-peer
mounts
.IR root / rank
on every rank and replicates the namespace. Precedence, lowest first: defaults, the program
name (the aliases DAGonFS_CS.exe and DAGonFS_P2P.exe), the configuration file, explicit options.
.PP
.B DAGonFS_Launcher
reads DAGonFS.ini (by default in its current directory) and runs mpirun with the configured
model, mount point and logging settings. Unmount the mount point (any peer's in peer-to-peer
mode) with fusermount3 \-u to stop the volume.
.SH POSIX OPERATIONS
The filesystem supports regular file and directory creation, lookup, reads, writes,
renames, links, symbolic links, metadata changes, extended attributes, statfs, and
the FUSE lifecycle operations. It reports no retained byte-range locks for getlk.
Extensions such as fallocate, ioctl, polling, and retained byte-range locks are not
provided.
.SH ADDITIONAL INFORMATION
Project documentation is available in the repository's docs directory.
